        <item>
            <title>1.2.11</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:02:04 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.2.11</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Recordings really do drag into CapCut now

1.2.10 said dragging a recording into CapCut worked. It only worked for
recordings CapCut had already imported. A new one still failed with
"Couldn't access some of the materials." Cubby now starts the drag the same
way Finder does, with the file itself, so a recording CapCut has never seen
drops in.

Screenshots and recent files drag the same way, and dragging no longer leaves
a copy of the file in your Library folder each time.

Dropping a recording or screenshot into a Finder folder now always copies it.
Before, it could move the file out of Cubby's folder, and that item would stop
working.
]]></description>
