        <item>
            <title>1.2.9</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:13:33 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.2.9</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### See a file before you paste it

When you press **←** for recent files, the preview now shows what's in the
highlighted file. Text files and code show their contents. PDFs, documents,
slides, images and videos show a Quick Look thumbnail, the same one Finder
draws. Anything Quick Look can't draw shows its icon, name and size.

### Paste several files at once

In the files list, press **⇧↑** or **⇧↓** to pick a run of files, or
**⌘-click** to add or remove one, then press **↩** to paste them all. Mail and
Messages attach every one. In a terminal they go in as quoted paths on one
line, ready for `mv`, `cp` or `git add`. **esc** drops the selection. You can
pick up to ten at a time.
]]></description>
